     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"font-size:15px;clear:both;font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:19.5px\">With R and Shiny Pro it is possible to implement multi-user analytical applications.</p><p style=\"font-size:15px;clear:both;font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:19.5px\">When a database is used to store intermediate data, how to give access to multiple user access to the db becomes very relevant and necessary.</p><p style=\"font-size:15px;clear:both;font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:19.5px\"><br></p><p style=\"font-size:15px;clear:both;font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:19.5px\">Currently I&#39;m using MonetDB / MonetDB.R configured (as usual for R) as a single user access, which means that any user operation occurs in sequence (users suddenly see that the app is not responsive and don&#39;t have a way to know why: e.g. the progress bar is user dependent.</p><p style=\"font-size:15px;clear:both;font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:19.5px\"><br></p><p style=\"font-size:15px;clear:both;font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:19.5px\">I would like to implement some type of connection pooling with the DB.</p><p style=\"font-size:15px;clear:both;font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:19.5px\">From past SO <a href=\"http://stackoverflow.com/questions/22155727/how-to-use-connection-pooling-for-monetdb\" style=\"color:rgb(12,101,165)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://stackoverflow.com/questions/22155727/how-to-use-connection-pooling-for-monetdb&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792397093500000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1naDShRICmOlCokMA69tbB\">responses</a> the driver does not include connection pooling.</p><p style=\"font-size:15px;clear:both;font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:19.5px\">Are there alternatives within these toolsets?</p><p style=\"font-size:15px;clear:both;font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:19.5px\"><br></p><p style=\"font-size:15px;clear:both;font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:19.5px\">I am starting to wonder if there is ANY similar connection-pooling implemented in any DB driver in R.  This could limit the kind of analytical apps that can be developed with R and Shiny...</p><p style=\"font-size:15px;clear:both;font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:19.5px\"><br></p><p style=\"font-size:15px;clear:both;font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:19.5px\">Any suggestion is welcome.</p><p style=\"font-size:15px;clear:both;font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:19.5px\"><br></p><p style=\"font-size:15px;clear:both;font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:19.5px\">(I posted this question in SO as well here <a href=\"http://stackoverflow.com/questions/32157446/connection-pooling-with-monetdb-r-and-shiny-pro\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://stackoverflow.com/questions/32157446/connection-pooling-with-monetdb-r-and-shiny-pro&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792397093500000&amp;usg=AOvVaw08QX4Yv5Ro8Lg5iJFrpU84\">http://stackoverflow.com/questions/32157446/connection-pooling-with-monetdb-r-and-shiny-pro</a>)</p><p style=\"font-size:15px;clear:both;font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;line-height:19.5px\"><br></p></div>"
